		"title": "The caller: a call to a name it does not define",
		"kind": "object",
		"command": "ld -o prog a.o b.o",
		"request": "a.o: .text writes the banner, then `e8 00 00 00 00` — a call whose displacement is still zero — followed by exit(eax). Its .symtab holds _start (defined) and `other` with st_shndx = SHN_UNDEF: a reference, not a definition. The .rela.text entry is an R_X86_64_PLT32 against `other` with addend -4",
		"request_hex": "",
		"response": "The linker resolves `other` to the definition b.o carries, and writes S + A - P into the four bytes at the call site: S is the output address of `other`, A is -4, P is the address of the displacement field itself",
